<BaseLayout title="About | Sepulchral Index"><article class="article"><div class="kicker">About</div><h1>An international underground publication from Chile.</h1><div class="article-content"><p>Sepulchral Index is a provisional name for an independent digital publication focused on extreme metal. Its purpose is simple: select, document and preserve worthwhile underground activity without attempting to cover everything.</p><p>The publication is based in Chile and gives particular attention to Chilean and South American scenes while remaining international in scope.</p><h2>Lineage</h2><p>The project grows from the editorial experience behind <strong>Burial Rituals News</strong>, a printed underground newsletter with sixteen issues, and exists in the same broader ecosystem as <strong>Oratorivm Records</strong>.</p><h2>Editorial independence</h2><p>Affiliation with Oratorivm is disclosed openly. Material released or distributed by Oratorivm does not receive preferential review treatment. Commercial relationships are disclosed when relevant, and releases issued directly by Oratorivm can be covered as news without being presented as scored or promotional reviews.</p></div></article></BaseLayout>
